          &lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Traditional varieties are often highly nutritious and have medicinal uses, for example in managing blood pressure and blood sugar.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;They are suited to local soils, can be grown with organic manure and without pesticides, and cope well with stresses such as erratic rainfall and drought.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;They can fetch higher market prices and need less labour.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;
          &lt;p&gt;A review of existing research on traditional rice varieties, covering their properties, the challenges facing them, and policy options.&lt;/p&gt;
          &lt;p&gt;Policies to protect and promote farmers' own varieties are needed to keep this genetic heritage and support sustainable agriculture. The review is aimed at farmers, seed producers and researchers.&lt;/p&gt;







