        Plain-language summary




          &lt;p&gt;Floods are becoming more frequent and severe in the Indian subcontinent. We mapped which areas are most likely to flood so that planners can prepare.&lt;/p&gt;
          &lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;A stacking ensemble, which combines several models, gave the best predictions (0.965).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;It was followed by XGBoost (0.934), a deep neural network (0.929), Random Forest (0.925), Logistic Regression (0.921) and SVM (0.920).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;
          &lt;p&gt;Past flood extents were mapped from Sentinel-1 radar images in Google Earth Engine, because radar can see through clouds. These records were used to train six machine learning models on 18 factors that influence flooding.&lt;/p&gt;
          &lt;p&gt;The flood susceptibility maps give city planners and disaster managers practical guidance on where to strengthen infrastructure and community resilience.&lt;/p&gt;







